      "heading": "A regular visit, not a legal inspection",
      "html": "<p>A walkround is a regular, written visit. You see conditions, talk to the workforce and spot problems. A CDM site inspection is a formal duty. The walkround is about presence and culture.</p><p>It is also not the pre-start check. That asks: is it safe to start today? The walkround looks at how the whole site is run. You need both.</p>"
