      "kind": "default",
      "eyebrow": "What to check",
      "heading": "Work the site in order",
      "html": "<p><strong>Tidiness first.</strong> Materials stored. Walkways and emergency routes clear. No trip hazards. Waste contained. A tidy site is usually a safe one.</p><p><strong>PPE.</strong> Hard hats, hi-vis, safety boots. Masks, face shields and gloves where the risk assessment asks. A PPE failure is a supervision failure.</p><p><strong>Access and height.</strong> Ladders footed or tied. Scaffold boards full, with edge protection. MEWP operators trained and harnessed. Falls from height are the top cause of deaths in UK construction.</p>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "default",
      "eyebrow": "Welfare, plant, permits",
      "heading": "The legal core",
      "html": "<p><strong>Welfare.</strong> The CDM Regulations 2015 require it. Enough clean toilets. Washing with hot and cold water. A rest area. Poor welfare risks prosecution.</p><p><strong>Plant.</strong> Operators certificated. LOLER and PUWER certificates in date. Look for damage, leaks and missing guards. Keep people clear of working plant.</p><p><strong>Signs and permits.</strong> Warning, PPE and emergency signs. A permit to work for hot work and confined spaces. Method statements and risk assessments on site, and read.</p>"
    },
