      "html": "<p>Were last walk's actions closed? Any new near misses? An empty near-miss board on a busy site is not good news. Nothing is reported. If managers ask about near misses, workers report them.</p><div class=\"checklist-box\"><ul><li>Last walk's actions: closed or carried forward</li><li>Near-miss board: reviewed, new entries looked into</li><li>Site edge and access: secure, signs in place</li><li>Walkways and emergency routes: clear</li><li>Tidiness: materials stored, waste controlled</li><li>PPE: right kit for the task</li><li>Ladders: right type, footed or tied</li><li>Scaffold: boarded, edge protected, toe boards, tag in date</li><li>MEWPs: trained operators, harnesses, exclusion zones</li><li>Welfare: toilets clean, washing available</li><li>Plant: operators certificated, certificates in date</li><li>Permits to work: in place for hazardous tasks</li><li>Method statements and risk assessments: on site and read</li><li>Safety signs: present and clear</li><li>First aid: first aider available, kit stocked</li><li>New actions: an owner and a date for each</li></ul></div>"
