      "heading": "Questions, answered",
      "html": "<h3>How is a walkround different from a CDM site inspection?</h3><p>A CDM inspection is formal, with legal duties and records. A walkround is a regular visit to see conditions and set standards. Less formal, equally useful.</p><h3>How often should I do a site walkround?</h3><p>There is no set number. Active sites often do one daily. A visiting advisor often does one weekly. Do it often enough to catch hazards before they cause harm.</p><h3>Who should do the walkround?</h3><p>The site manager, the principal contractor's H&amp;S advisor, or both. Subcontractor supervisors should walk their own areas. It works best with someone who can stop unsafe work.</p><h3>Should I share findings with the whole team?</h3><p>Yes. Share them, with near misses, at the toolbox talk or on the board. That changes behaviour more than a report in a folder.</p>"
